sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor A as Browser (Device A)
  participant N as nginx (TLS, rate limit)
  participant API as API (Hono on Bun)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (Prisma)
  participant WS as Socket.IO Gateway
  actor B as Browser (Device B)

  Note over A: device_id minted once and kept in localStorage

  A->>N: POST /api/auth/login {identifier, password, deviceId}
  N->>N: limit_req 30/min per address
  N->>API: proxy_pass
  API->>API: ipRestriction, CORS, CSRF
  API->>DB: find by university_id OR phone_number
  DB-->>API: user row + password_hash
  API->>API: argon2id verify (worker thread)

  alt account not APPROVED, or is_active = false
    API-->>A: 403 with the reason in Persian
  else credentials valid
    API->>DB: revoke every session whose device_id differs
    API->>DB: upsert session, set users.device_id
    DB-->>API: session id (sid)
    API->>API: sign access (15 min) + refresh (7 days), two secrets
    API-->>A: 200 + access_token, refresh_token, session_hint cookies
    API->>WS: disconnectDevice(userId, oldDeviceId)
    WS--)B: socket closed
  end

  A->>WS: WebSocket handshake (cookies attached by the browser)
  WS->>DB: verify token, session, device
  WS-->>A: connected, joined every chat room

  Note over B: the old device still holds a token bound to the old device

  B->>API: GET /api/chats (stale cookie)
  API->>DB: session lookup by sid
  DB-->>API: users.device_id no longer matches token.did
  API-->>B: 401 DEVICE_MISMATCH
  Note over B: the client skips refresh and routes to /login?device=...
